Render only the pages the schedule actually shows.

server.py builds all five pages unconditionally, so every regeneration launches
Chromium five times even when the schedule names one. On a Pi Zero 2 W that is
roughly 40 seconds per page: three or four minutes of thrashing instead of one
render.

Applied by upstream/install-on-pi.sh with `git apply`, which fails loudly if
upstream moves this code rather than silently doing nothing.

diff --git a/server/server.py b/server/server.py
index 3c89087..d71924a 100644
--- a/server/server.py
+++ b/server/server.py
@@ -231,6 +231,16 @@ def main():
         DailyPage(*geometry),
         TomorrowPage(*geometry),
     ]
+    # Each page is a separate Chromium run. Keep only what the schedule shows.
+    scheduled = {
+        image
+        for pool in cfg.schedule.describe().get("pools", {}).values()
+        for image in pool
+    }
+    if scheduled:
+        pages = [page for page in pages if f"{page.name}.png" in scheduled]
+        log.info("rendering %d of 5 pages: %s",
+                 len(pages), ", ".join(page.name for page in pages))
     # map_url is a constant, so it comes from a StaticSource; the weather
     # service supplies the rest. Each page declares what it needs in
     # Page.requires.
